# ---------------- Civilian.events (Task 16 Part I: non-hostile bystander) ----------------
# TK4's civilian: unarmed, never attacks, wanders calmly — and bolts the moment it is shot.
# Every number comes from `enemy type "Civilian"` (EnemyTypes.events); this sheet only says
# what a civilian *does*, so retuning civilians is a data-file edit.
#
# Being the one type with `my Hostile false` is load-bearing: the enemy sheets check that flag
# before chasing or attacking, and `when all enemies dead` (Task 16 Part G) ignores
# non-hostile actors — a level can be cleared with civilians still running around.

when me appears
  enemy type "Civilian"
  set my mode to "calm"
  # Run at twice the type's walking pace, so a shot visibly changes the civilian's speed.
  set my FleeSpeed to my Speed + 70
  wander speed my Speed

# Shot: spray, count the damage, then turn away from the shooter and run. `other` is the
# projectile (or whoever sent `"damage"`), so facing it puts the civilian's back to the threat
# and the new, faster wander leg carries them off.
when message "damage" arrives
  spawn Blood at me
  set my LastDmg to other's damage
  set my Health to my Health - my LastDmg
  set my mode to "flee"
  face other
  wander speed my FleeSpeed

when my Health becomes 0
  spawn Gib at me offset 0
  spawn Gib at me offset 12
  spawn Gib at me offset -12
  destroy me
